{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 16, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "\"the social network\" is a movie that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the consequences that followed. the film is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich.\n\nthe movie starts with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, a sophomore at harvard, who is dumped by his girlfriend, erica albright, played by rachel meyer. this event sparks mark's idea to create a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the website becomes an instant hit, but also gets mark into trouble with the university administration.\n\nmark then meets with the winklevoss twins, played by armie hammer, who are also harvard students and want to create a social networking site for their university. they enlist mark's help, but he eventually betrays them and creates his own site, \"thefacebook\", with the help of his friend eduardo saverin, played by andrew garfield.\n\nas \"thefacebook\" gains popularity, mark and eduardo's friendship begins to fray, and they become embroiled in a series of lawsuits and disputes over the ownership and direction of the company. meanwhile, mark's relationships with his friends and family begin to deteriorate, and he becomes increasingly isolated and focused on his creation.\n\nthe movie is notable for its sharp dialogue and witty banter, courtesy of aaron sorkin's script. the cast delivers strong performances, with jesse eisenberg bringing a nuanced and complex portrayal to the role of mark zuckerberg. andrew garfield is also impressive as eduardo saverin, capturing the character's charm and vulnerability.\n\nthe film's cinematography is sleek and modern, capturing the sterile and privileged atmosphere of harvard and the early days of facebook. david fincher's direction is masterful, using a range of techniques to convey the frenetic pace and intensity of mark's world.\n\none of the most interesting aspects of \"the social network\" is its exploration of the themes of ambition, friendship, and the consequences of success. mark zuckerberg is portrayed as a complex and multifaceted character, driven by a mix of motivations including a desire for recognition, a need for revenge, and a passion for innovation.\n\noverall, \"the social network\" is a compelling and thought-provoking movie that offers a fascinating glimpse into the early days of facebook and the personalities that shaped it. it's a film that will appeal to anyone interested in technology, entrepreneurship, or the complexities of human relationships.", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.6315475702285767}, {"token": "the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " social", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -5.125986263010418e-06}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -2.719341516494751}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.002334371441975236}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.8362528681755066}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -2.9802276912960224e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -6.198863957251888e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.1269303560256958}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.0014642480527982116}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.00012337400403339416}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.6931471824645996}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -9.60780744208023e-05}, {"token": " consequences", "logprob": -0.14353878796100616}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -1.311301275563892e-06}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.22140826284885406}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -3.540453326422721e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.3215617835521698}, {"token": " film"